(2) What do the witnesses force on the edge itself?  For an edge (a,c), a witness x forces
    GAP      : a.e < c.s strictly   (makes 'meets' impossible)   e.g. BEFORE(a,x)+BEFORE(x,c)
    NOGAP    : a.e >= c.s           (makes 'before with a gap' impossible)
    SAMEEND  / NOTSAMEEND / SAMESTART / NOTSAMESTART likewise.
    Each witness is evaluated with only its two edges (the edge itself is left unlabelled);
    readings of the other labels: BASE above, BEGINS-ON=same-start, ENDS-ON=unconstrained (to avoid circularity).
